</font></ul></td></tr></table><table cellpadding=2 cellspacing=1 border=0 width=100%><tr bgcolor=#336699><td><font size=2 face=verdana
color=gold><b>Alternate Characters</b></font> - <font size=1 face=verdana
color=white><a href=/showmember.php?name=Jiggles>Jiggles</a> on
<font color=#ffff00>Sun February 4th, 2001 12:58pm</font></font></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#ddddff><td><ul><font size=1 face=verdana>I have changed a few things around here on the website.  You must now log in via your main character only, and not alternates.  Please let me know which characters that are currently 'Member' status are actuall alternates to your main character.  This is so that we can get a real goodhandle of hoe many live bodies are behind the characters.  You can also add your own alternates (only if they are a guild member) to the website member list.-Jiggles
</font></ul></td></tr></table><table cellpadding=2 cellspacing=1 border=0 width=100%><tr bgcolor=#336699><td><font size=2 face=verdana
color=gold><b>Website changes</b></font> - <font size=1 face=verdana
color=white><a href=/showmember.php?name=Jiggles>Jiggles</a> on
<font color=#ffff00>Sun January 28th, 2001 4:12pm</font></font></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#ddddff><td><ul><font size=1 face=verdana>Ok, few changes are occuring, so if you run into an error, let me know.<p>First off, I am seperating members from their alterate characters.  You can no longer log into your \"Alternates\" account, so you should log into your main account.  This is so we can have a good handhold on how many members we actually have.<p>I have also made a Member profile page, where you can look at the individual members in detail.<p>You can now upload an image for your profile, and you can put in some roleplaying information.<p>Lastly, all posts to the forums no longer show your email address.  If you click on someone's name, it will show their profile.<p>Anyhow, hope everyone likes the changes.   - Jiggles
</font></ul></td></tr></table><table cellpadding=2 cellspacing=1 border=0 width=100%><tr bgcolor=#336699><td><font size=2 face=verdana
color=gold><b>Leadership Council</b></font> - <font size=1 face=verdana
color=white><a href=/showmember.php?name=Jiggles>Jiggles</a> on
<font color=#ffff00>Thu January 25th, 2001 11:12pm</font></font></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#ddddff><td><ul><font size=1 face=verdana>I have updated the members page to portray the correct form of leadership within the guild.  In most guilds, the position of 'Guild Leader' is totalitarian, owned by one individual.  Here in Norrath Militia, the founding members have chosen a method of leadership where major guild related changes are left up to the founding members of guild (Leadership Council) and its officers.  There is not one single leader amongst us, but many.  I hope this clears up any confusion we have had in the past of 'Who is the guild leader?'-Jiggles
</font></ul></td></tr></table><table cellpadding=2 cellspacing=1 border=0 width=100%><tr bgcolor=#336699><td><font size=2 face=verdana
